gm-method (LoadingMachine: fallback after: must be gated, not unconditional; 5-flag boolean conjunction with no timeout is fatal): ROOT CAUSE of deployed-no-world-until-refresh: gating loadingScreen.hide() on a 5-flag boolean conjunction with NO timeout -- when any flag never fires (ModelPool engagement race, streamed entity loads without onMeshReady), the curtain stays up over a fully-rendered world. Fix: an xstate machine with a fallback after: timeout (10s soft stop, 45s hard unconditional) that reaches ready when all flags done OR fallback fires. The soft after: must be gated on hasContent (firstSnapshot && environment), not unconditional, or it lifts the curtain before the slow gh-pages worker connects.